<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $94.9 mln March 26.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $94.9 mln March 26.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $94.9 million surplus on March 26 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 26</p>
<p>Exports: $262.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $278.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $368.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $256.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $94.9 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.803 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.878 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.223 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.977 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $171 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
